WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:02.290
(violin harmonics music)

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:05.200
- My grandmother, if she
knew now what I was making,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.110
would be very surprised.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.750
Mochi is originally from Japan.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.130
It's a white pastry that's
made from rice flour.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.660
It's stuffed with azuki beans.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.602
That's the traditional mochi.

00:00:17.602 --> 00:00:20.890
Our mochi has become Hawaiian mochi.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.363
My own style.

00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:25.130
(soothing violin music)

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.200
We live in Hawaii and, if you look around,

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.100
we have deserts and snow,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.540
we have tropical rainforests
and all the flowers,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.380
the birds and the oceans—
it's all very colorful.

00:00:44.843 --> 00:00:48.343
(serene orchestral music)

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.880
This is Hilo Town.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.610
I would consider it to be old Hawaii.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.020
Everything is a little bit slower.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.113
Hilo is where I grew up
and where my grandparents

00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:04.310
settled when they first came from Japan.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.930
They came as workers for the
plantation in the cane fields.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.260
They were seeking a
better life, and so did

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.210
the other groups of people that came

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.610
from all over the world.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.352
Filipinos, Chinese, Koreans, they all

00:01:18.352 --> 00:01:21.710
had to live together, and
they all shared their food.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.360
The Japanese contribution was the mochi.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.770
Every time I taste it, I think back

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:33.840
to where I came from, and
I think of my grandma.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.510
She, as a treat, would make her mochi.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.300
Her mochi was the reason
that I had interest

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.490
to keep mochi on the menu of Hawaii.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.230
(solemn piano music)

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.190
Two Ladies Kitchen is called Two Ladies

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:54.150
because we started with
just my aunt and myself.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.170
I knew that my aunt knew how to make mochi

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.220
but there was nobody
else to pass it on to.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.160
And I knew that mochi is my calling.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.530
When I first started the
business, it was just

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.930
my family who helped me.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.340
My parents are now in their 90s,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.300
and they still come to the mochi shop.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.100
A lot of our flavors are found in Hawaii.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.470
We have a strawberry mochi,
with a fresh strawberry

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.880
on top of the beans and it's
wrapped in the white mochi.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.330
That is very popular.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.890
Liliko'i is passion fruit,
so I use the fresh nectar

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.090
and we make mochi.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.830
We use the fruits of the season,

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.830
persimmons, peaches and nectarines,

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.910
pineapple, on and on.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:38.242
Now I have a ginger mochi, brownie mochi,

00:02:38.242 --> 00:02:41.560
a marshmallow, like a rocky road.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.850
I never say no to someone's suggestion.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.792
It's been almost 25 years, and now,

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:50.560
we have lines out the door.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.417
It's not only the Japanese people

00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:56.750
who embrace mochi, but it's
become a Hawaiian food.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.270
I meet people from all over the world,

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.100
and they, too, now love mochi.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.020
It sticks everyone together,

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:08.870
other races, culture, our family friends.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.300
Mochi just makes you feel happy,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.550
and that's why I say, “Mochi is love.”

